// D-CONF-PLANE1/D-CONF-NAME1 (card #1517): `outputs:` names the runnable
// artifact and the checked function that defines it. A single-segment
// `entry: run` can never prove `outputs:` drives anything — resolving it
// runs the exact same "one root-level file with a top-level `fn run`" scan
// as the migration-era fallback, so it always finds the same file whether
// `outputs:` exists or not. The dotted form `entry: service.run` is
// different in kind: it names the package member file `service/service.jet`
// (D-MOD-CYCLE1=A: a package is one namespace, so an entry names a member
// file by its stem), a file the fallback structurally cannot reach (it only
// ever scans root-level files). Delete `outputs:` here and `jet run`/`jet
// build` stop resolving an entry at all — see `tests/package_outputs.rs`'s
// negative test.
name: "outputs_build_demo"
version: "0.1.0"
outputs: { demo: .Executable{ entry: service.run } }
authority: { holds: { allow: [IO] } }
